No extra carrier is added to this table; the existing and planned working stocks already introduce DEP 1360 mg, TEC 720 mg, DPG 326.666667 mg, ethanol 70 mg and IPM 23.333333 mg = 2500 mg. Do not add these carrier totals a second time.

Ambrox Super uses the actual 25% w/w stock (3 g product + 7 g DPG + 0.5 g IPM + 1.5 g ethanol). Tonkarome uses 20% w/w TEC (4 g product + 16 g TEC). Alpha Irone uses 10% w/w DEP. All other “neat” entries mean the owned stock as supplied, not an assay of purity.

## Nominal bottle target, after holds clear

Measure 6.00 mL homogeneous concentrate and permitted ethanol q.s. to a measured final 30.00 mL. This is 20% v/v raw-stock concentrate, not 20% pure odorants. Do not assume this 6.500 g master occupies 6.000 mL or has enough volume before measurement. Uniform scaling is permitted arithmetically; a different stock strength needs an explicit active-dose rebase.

Actual finished ppm requires measured aliquot and final bottle masses. Owned “96% ethanol” percentage basis is unresolved. No physical compounding, skin use, safety, stability, similarity or performance approval has been issued.

**First computational question:** how robust is the separate Ebanol-accent allocation alongside Sandalore under source reconciliation, uncertainty analysis and whole-mixture comparison? Any virtual alternatives stay internal. The handoff is one final formula for a whole-blend test; no separate physical omission is required before that handoff. This card is not a sensory-validated winner.
